<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    Kuna #1627: "x86-64: SENDUIPI decodes as RDRAND; VGATHERPF0DPS reads a GPR
    index"  https://github.com/Noelo-Lab/kuna/issues/1627

    Bytes (the issue's repro, as clang assembles it):
      f30fc7f7              senduipi %rdi            -> was RDRAND EDI
      0f183d40000000        prefetchit0 0x40(%rip)   -> was NOP/reserved
      62f27d49c60c88        vgatherpf0dps (%rax,%zmm1,4){%k1}
                                                     -> index was RCX, operand a loaded dword
      c3                    ret
      f30f01ec f30f01ed f30f01ee f30f01ef   uiret testui clui stui
                                            (clui/stui were RDPKRU/WRPKRU)
      0fc7f7                rdrand %edi (control: the unprefixed form stays RDRAND)

    Stage: S1 decode-table / S2 p-code lift (x86 spec-fix, no option).  The
    UINTR group lives in uintr.sinc, PREFETCHIT0/1 in ia.sinc ahead of the
    0F 18 NOP group, and the eight VGATHERPF constructors use the vsib
    operand tables (vm32z/vm64z/vm32y) like VSCATTERPF already did, so the
    user-op receives the gather address, not a dword loaded through a GPR.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">
f30fc7f70f183d4000000062f27d49c60c88c3
f30f01ecf30f01edf30f01eef30f01ef
0fc7f7
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="f"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>disassemble 0x1000 0x1026</com>
  <com>parse line extern void f(unsigned long target);</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
